<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Status bar icon. Android keeps only the alpha and tints the rest, so the white below is
  a placeholder. Every tile edge is a whole unit of the 24 grid, which is pixel aligned at
  every density except hdpi.

  No panel border. A one unit stroke is thinner than a pixel at the size a status bar draws,
  and it crowds the gaps between the tiles it surrounds.

  Cells are 6 wide with 1 between them, inside a margin of 2. With every edge on a whole
  unit and equal margins on both sides, 6 is as large as a three by three grid gets.

  Kept in step with art/icon-notification.svg.
-->
